In a previous article, rowewl@ucunix.san.uc.edu (William L. Rowe) says:

>
>Hi,  I am looking for a new vesion of nethack for a friend.  She has
>version 3.0 already, and is looking for a new version.  She says that
>this version crashes in one of the mazes at a certain level.  Are there
>any fixes for this problem or is there a new version???? Version 4.0 or
>so.  Any help would be greatly appreciated. Bill Perry
>Rowewl@ucunix.san.uc.edu
>   

	The latest available version of nethack for MS-DOS is
version 3.0j, a.k.a. version 3.0, patchlevel 10. It is available
via anonymous FTP from linc.cis.upenn.edu.
	In my experience, NetHack 3.0 has always been very stable
and crash-free; perhaps your friend's installation could use some
adjustment. NetHack requires more and more free disk space as
the game advances, so if the game crashes at about the same
dungeon level each time, you may need to free up some space.
The game can consume something close to an additional megabyte
of space before you near completion.
	You should definetely check out the group rec.games.hack,
which is dedicated to the game of NetHack.

